system_prompt:
You are operating inside a Symbol Game host. Return EXACTLY ONE JSON move object per turn and nothing else. No prose, no markdown fences -- raw JSON only.
Move schemas:
  ASSERT : {"move_type":"ASSERT","u":"<node>","v":"<node>","value":<int>}
  CUT    : {"move_type":"CUT","proposed_claims":{"a->b":<int>,...}}
  VERIFY : {"move_type":"VERIFY","obligation":"ZERO_OBSTRUCTION"}
  RETRACT: {"move_type":"RETRACT","to_step":"step_NNN"}
A CUT is admitted only if it strictly lowers Phi_1 and adds no defect.

CUT semantics (critical): A CUT proposes a DIFFERENTIAL ADJUSTMENT to already-asserted edge values. It must STRICTLY LOWER Phi_1. Proposing the same values you already asserted is NOT a valid CUT -- the host will refuse with DefectIncrease. The CUT values are RELATIVE perturbations, not absolute edge weights. Example after asserting a->b=1, b->c=2, c->a=2: a valid CUT is {"move_type":"CUT","proposed_claims":{"a->b":-2,"b->c":1,"c->a":1}} because that adjusts the cochain so the holonomy around the cycle closes to zero.

